course: dictionary
lesson: 8525
title: One word, two meanings
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Many words have more than one meaning. A sausage is minced meat with spices, put inside a long thin skin and cooked. But informally, sausage is also a fond name for a child or a pet. «You silly sausage!» is said with love, not to say the person is a meal.
explain: How do you know which meaning is right? Read the words around it. In «They hunt and find sardines, biscuits and a sausage», the list is all food, so sausage means the food. In «You silly sausage!» someone is being teased kindly, so it is a name.
explain: Context can also tell you about place. «Let's go to the servo for a snag!» Rian does not know that a snag is a sausage, and a servo is a petrol station. When you are not sure, test your meaning in the sentence. If it still makes sense, you have found the right one.
fact: A sausage is minced meat with spices, put inside a long thin skin and cooked.
fact: Informally, sausage can be a fond name for a child or pet, as in «You silly sausage!»
fact: «A sausage at a barbecue is mostly minced pork, and pork is meat from a pig.»
fact: A sausage dog is a dachshund, and a sausage roll is a sausage wrapped in pastry.
fact: In Australia, a sausage sizzle is a barbecue that raises money for schools.
exercise: «They hunt and find sardines, biscuits and a sausage.» What does sausage mean here? | A fond name for a child | A petrol station | *Minced meat with spices, put in a long thin skin and cooked | A type of dog
exercise: «You silly sausage!» says Mum to her little boy, with a smile. What does sausage mean here? | Minced meat in a skin | *A fond name, showing she loves him | A petrol station
exercise: Rian hears «Let's go to the servo for a snag!» What is a snag? | A petrol station | *A sausage | A kind of dog | A bread roll
test: What is a sausage dog? | A sausage with a long tail | *A dachshund | A barbecue that raises money | A petrol station
test: Which sentence uses sausage as a fond name? | «Dad cooked sausages for tea.» | *«Oh, you little sausage, come here!» | «The sausages sizzled in the pan.» | «Pork is meat from a pig.»
exam: Which words in «A sausage at a barbecue is mostly minced pork» show that sausage means food? | Sausage and mostly | *Barbecue and minced pork | A and is | Pork and pig
